# Paths clang-format skips, matched against the path relative to this file.
#
# The syntax resembles .gitignore but is not it, in two ways worth knowing before editing:
# `*` does not cross a path separator, so a bare `*.in` matches only at the top level and a
# pattern meant to apply at any depth needs a leading `**/`, which also covers zero directories
# and so subsumes the bare form. A leading `/` does not anchor — it simply fails to match.
# Verified against clang-format 22.

# CMake configure_file templates. Not compilable C++ — the @VAR@ placeholders are substituted
# at configure time — so clang-format parses them as C++ and reformats around the substitutions.
**/*.in

# Third-party sources. clang-format does not read .gitignore, so a recursive -i over the tree
# would otherwise rewrite every dependency CPM has fetched.
.cpm-cache/**
build*/**
